<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indonesian independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Indonesian independence was proclaimed in 1945 and recognised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> in 1949 after a period of armed conflict and negotiation. It ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a>. The loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> was the decisive blow to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence.jpg" alt="Indonesian independence" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frans Mendur (also Frans Mendoer) (1913 – 1971) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indonesia_declaration_of_independence_17_August_1945.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
